{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939387-proximi-clash-of-wills-rules","id":939387,"title":"Proximi: Clash of Wills rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T00:26:43-07:00","id":939387,"title":"Proximi: Clash of Wills rules?","content":"So, Proximi are awesome, moreso now that we know they'll have 1 free Reach on all their Blessings with the new Errata. One issue which does not appear to have been addressed, though, is what happens when a Proximus Blessing is contested by another power that provokes a Clash of Wills. A Mage's spell would do Arcanum + Gnosis, but Proximi explicitly have neither trait, so what do they use instead (if anything)? Do they just use a chance die? Automatically fail any Clash? Roll Resolve or Composure (because both would be flipping broken)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11673-corwyn_ulhar","name":"Corwyn_Ulhar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T01:02:35-07:00","id":939397,"title":"","content":"As most of the splats use Power Stat + Ability Dot, which usually is also a &quot;dicepool for using the power in question&quot;, we arrived at conclusion that we will use Willpower for Clash of Proximi Will. <br /> It makes them really strong at their Blessing, so if you are aiming at a game where they are supposed to be less powerful, you might consider using higher of their Resolve/Composure. If you want to get little more un-standard, make them roll their *current willpower points*, not their Willpower Dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:18:47-07:00","id":939456,"title":"","content":"I'd either give them an appropriate resistance attribute or have the dot rating of the blessing as their dice pool. Essentially still treats it as power stat + magic dot rating or attribute, but proximi have 0 in power stat like all mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:36:33-07:00","id":939462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corwyn_Ulhar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939387-proximi-clash-of-wills-rules#post939387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Proximi are awesome, moreso now that we know they'll have 1 free Reach on all their Blessings with the new Errata. One issue which does not appear to have been addressed, though, is what happens when a Proximus Blessing is contested by another power that provokes a Clash of Wills. A Mage's spell would do Arcanum + Gnosis, but Proximi explicitly have neither trait, so what do they use instead (if anything)? Do they just use a chance die? Automatically fail any Clash? Roll Resolve or Composure (because both would be flipping broken)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The dot rating of the Blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}